  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), three-quarter view of the right-hand SCG Premium grip on the Omni Throttle adapter, grip lying sideways with the head to the left, thumb side (hats, red A2, white C1 wheel) and the GNX EVO base control panel visible; the far side of the grip (B1, triggers, D1) is hidden - placed on gallery-3",
  "mappingSource": "EDCD community button map 231D3200 (https://github.com/EDCD/EliteCustomButtonNames/blob/main/files/INTO%20Bindings/DeviceButtonMaps/231D3200.buttonMap, VKB factory profile) as cited by the catalog; control names and places from VKB's binding template \"VKB Gladiator SCG OTA (RH)\" v1.0 by UntoldForce (https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0808/7827/2731/files/VKB-Gladiator-SCG-OTA-RH-v1.0_9bbaacdb-cf89-4ada-ba39-7f228206d676.pdf, linked on https://vkbsimcontrollers.com/pages/downloads) - drawn on this same photo, leader lines with labels only, no button numbers",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "template leaders on this photo: A4 (Top Right Hat) = ribbed hat on top of the head; A3 (Center Hat) = the cross-shaped cap (printed \"A3\" next to it); A1 (Ministick) = knurled round cap at the lower left of the head; A2 = red button; C1 (Thumb Hat) = white ribbed wheel-hat on the grip. A3/A4 numbering is uncertain: the EDCD map names BTN6-10 \"A3\" and BTN11-15 \"A4\" but its POVs say POV2=A4, POV3=A3 - both hats are candidates only (same finding as for vkb-gnx-evo-scg-premium-right). throttle.axis.main (JOY_Z): EDCD names Joy_ZAxis \"Throttle\"; JOY_Z is also present on the plain SCG Premium (231D0200) where it is the base centre throttle wheel, so the catalog's \"Omni Throttle adds the throttle lever on JOY_Z\" is doubtful - JOY_Z is most likely the base wheel, and the Omni Throttle's own push/pull travel is a gimbal axis. Marked as a candidate on the base wheel. Sw1 = left wheel with the tab (printed Sw1), En1 = right wheel; EDCD calls BTN25/26 \"En2\", the template \"Sw1 (Base Left Side)\". Base buttons: template order F2/F1/F3 = left/centre/right (F2 printed next to the left button).",
